# Graphify usage

- Use `rg` and targeted file reading for routine code search, roadmap/status questions, concrete
  bugs, and normal single-repository work.
- Run Graphify only when the user explicitly writes `/graphify`, or for a genuinely large
  cross-repository architecture investigation where relationship traversal materially helps.
- Do not run Graphify just because `graphify-out/` exists or has uncommitted files. Do not run
  `graphify update .` after ordinary changes.
- After every Graphify run, identify its Python processes by command line, stop only positively
  identified Graphify-owned processes if they remain, and verify they exited. Never stop an
  unrelated Python process.
